<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baltasar Maldonado</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1552">1552</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baltasar Maldonado was a Spanish conquistador in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, in present-day Colombia. A captain in the conquest of the Muisca lands, in 1539 he led the expedition against Tundama, the ruler of Duitama, who had resisted Spanish rule. He defeated Tundama's forces at the battle of Bonza, ending one of the last major Muisca resistances to Spanish rule.</p></div>
